.TH mnnn-net-exchange 1  "mnnn-net-exchange 2.7.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-net\-exchange \- Key exchanges with other nodes
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn net exchange\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Key exchanges with other nodes
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-create(1)
Offer a key exchange: prints a token to pass on, or sends it with \-\-peer
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-accept(1)
Accept an offer (incoming exchange id or token), or complete ours with an answer token
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-list(1)
Key exchanges
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-show(1)
One exchange, with its short code and fingerprint
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-verify(1)
Confirm the short code the other side read out
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-revoke(1)
End an exchange: the key is erased here and the peer is told
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-label(1)
Rename an exchange
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-export(1)
Write an encrypted backup of the node identity and all exchanges
.TP
mnnn\-net\-exchange\-restore(1)
Restore exchanges (and the node identity) from a backup
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.7.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
